<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84331" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιμήν</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ένος</span>, ὁ, voc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιμήν</span>
		(not <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μέν</span>) Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			2.717
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>herdsman,</i> whether of sheep or oxen, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.82
			</span></i>-<i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>, al.; opp. lord or owner (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄναξ</span>),
				<i><span class="en">
				4.87
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> after <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always <i>shepherd,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουκόλοι καὶ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					714
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				281
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				174d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				343a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				735b
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. προβάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ge.</u>
					4.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>shepherd</i> of the people, regularly of Agamemnon, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀγαμέμνονα π. λαῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.243
				</span></i>
			, al.: generally, <i>captain, chief,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				85
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				360
			</span></i> codd. (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῶν ποιμένες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					767
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόχων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1140
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄχων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					674
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιμένες δώρων Κυπρίας,</span>
			of the Loves, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				8.6
			</span></i>: abs., <i>master, lord,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοῦτος ὁ λαχὼν ποιμένα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>O.</u>
					10(11).88
				</span></i>
			; for <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				657
			</span></i>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρόβος.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				LXX
			</span></i> and <i>NT, pastor, teacher, Je.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				2.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Eph.</u>
				4.11
			</span></i>, etc. (Cf.Lith.<i>piemuõ,</i> gen.sg.
				<i>piemeñs</i> 'shepherd'.)</div>
